From 80f0d52334d0c9e0203995f270015fee7d511191 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:24:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] hw/sensor: add an ICM20608 six-axis IMU model (ecspi3)
 for the AES board
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Register-file teaching model for the TDK ICM20608 on ecspi3: bit7-of-
address R/W framing with auto-increment, config registers as storage,
data window 0x3b..0x48 derived from seven injectable uint16 QOM
properties (accel-x/y/z, gyro-x/y/z, temp), WHO_AM_I answers 0xAF.

Framing note: the ECSPI controller exchanges whole 32-bit FIFO words,
so short transactions arrive padded with leading zero bytes; the state
machine therefore keys on the address byte itself (bit7 set starts a
read) rather than transaction boundaries — the pad bytes fall into the
harmless write branch. SSIPeripheralClass::realize is mandatory (the
base class calls it unconditionally) — provide a no-op.

mcimx6ul-evk attaches one on the ecspi3 SSI bus (SoC child spi[2]).

Verified with the imxaes teaching driver (Linux v7.1, module insmod):
probe succeeds, and the SPI byte stream seen by the model carries the
injected sample data exactly (az=0x0800 at +-16g = 1g, temp raw 250).
Known issue: the guest still reads zeros through the driver because the
imx_spi model packs the 4-byte exchange words differently than the
kernel spi-imx driver expects — the controller-side word packing needs
a quirk, tracked as follow-up work.
